00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:00.279
I have been taking
the New York subway

00:03:00.279 --> 00:03:02.247
since I first moved here
in 1997.

00:03:02.247 --> 00:03:05.985
I remember when I first started
on "Weekend Update,"

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:09.222
and I was like, "Wow, people are
probably going to freak out

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:14.294
when they see me on the subway,
because I'm kind of on TV now."

00:03:14.294 --> 00:03:17.864
I was, like,
looking around the car,

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:20.767
waiting for someone
to recognize me.

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:22.768
Guess what?
No one cares.

00:03:22.768 --> 00:03:25.304
No one cared then,
and no one cares now.

00:03:25.304 --> 00:03:26.772
And that's why I love
New York.

00:03:26.772 --> 00:03:28.941
They don't care who's on TV,
who's not on TV.

00:03:28.941 --> 00:03:31.444
Everyone's a star.
It's New York City.

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:35.848
No one cares.

